● Both done.

  The 5.10 break

  lib/Matplotlib/Simple.pm:2625 in venn_proportional_area used each @keys.
  each/keys/values on an array arrived in 5.12 — under 5.10 it's a compile-time
  error, which is why every test file aborted in BEGIN. Replaced with an index
  loop:

  foreach my $i ( 0 .. $#keys ) { # "each @array" requires perl 5.12
        my $key  = $keys[$i];
        my $name = "venn_ax${ax}_set$i";
        ...

  I swept the rest of the file for other post-5.10 syntax (s///r, postfix deref,
  %h{...} slices, signatures, __SUB__, keys $hashref, package NAME { }, fc) —
  that each was the only one. List::Util qw(max sum min) and Scalar::Util 
  'looks_like_number' are all fine at 5.10's bundled versions.

  Verified: 208 tests pass under perl-5.10.1 (Result: PASS), same under 5.44.0.

  test.all.perls.pl

  Modeled on ~/Scripts/stats/test.all.perls.pl, adapted for a pure-Perl dist:

  - --syntax / -c — compiles lib/*.pm + t/*.t under each perl and stops. 0.6s
  for all three perls versus 69s for the full cycle, and it's the mode that
  still works on a perl missing prerequisites. This is the mode that catches
  exactly the class of bug above.
  - Full mode drops the XS-specific OPTIMIZE=-Wall and always runs perl -c on
  the module before Makefile.PL/make/make test, so a syntax regression reports
  in a tenth of a second instead of after a build.
  - DEPS vs FAIL — a perl that can't load IPC::System::Simple is reported
  separately from a perl that rejects your code, including autodie's "X required
  for Fatalised..." phrasing which doesn't say "Can't locate". --deps cpanms
  them.
  - Scrapes PREREQ_PM, MIN_PERL_VERSION and VERSION from Makefile.PL
  (dzil-generated, so it tracks dist.ini); perls below MIN_PERL_VERSION report
  SKIP unless --all.
  - Checks python3/matplotlib once up front — it's shared by every perl, so a
  broken python would otherwise look like N identical regressions.
  - Optional Perl::MinimumVersion advisory pass that names the computed floor
  and flags it if it exceeds the declared MIN_PERL_VERSION (currently not
  installed here, so it says so and moves on — cpanm Perl::MinimumVersion under
  5.44 enables it).
  - --install now defaults off (the stats version installs by default);
  installing this into every perlbrew perl seemed like the wrong default. Logs
  go to .build/multiperl/, which I added to .gitignore.

  The script is itself written to compile under 5.10.1, so it can run under the
  old perl it's testing.

  Two things I did not do, since you didn't ask: no $VERSION/Changes bump for
  the release that carries this fix, and the stale copies under
  Matplotlib-Simple-0.31/ still contain the old each @keys (dzil regenerates
  those).

