      284  
      285  ## Barplot/bar/barh
      286  
      287 -Plot a hash or a hash of arrays as a boxplot                  
      287 +Plot a hash, a hash of arrays, or a hash of hashes as a bar ch
          +art.  `bar` draws                                             
      288 +vertical bars, `barh` horizontal ones; every option below appl
          +ies to both.                                                  
      289  
      290 +### Entering data                                             
      291 +                                                              
      292 +`data` accepts three shapes, and the shape alone decides wheth
          +er you get one                                                
      293 +bar per key or a group of bars per key:                       
      294 +                                                              
      295 +**1. One bar per key (hash of numbers).** The simplest case — 
          +the key is the                                                
      296 +tick label:                                                   
      297 +                                                              
      298 +    bar(                                                      
      299 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/simple.svg',                       
      300 +     data          => { Mon => 73, Tue => 93, Wed => 77 },     
      301 +    );                                                        
      302 +                                                              
      303 +**2. Groups of bars (hash of array refs).** Each key becomes a
          + group; index `i`                                             
      304 +of every array is one series, so `color` and `label` are array
          +s indexed the same                                            
      305 +way:                                                          
      306 +                                                              
      307 +    bar(                                                      
      308 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/grouped.svg',                      
      309 +     data          => {                                        
      310 +             1941 => [ 6.6, 6.2 ],    # UK, US                         
      311 +             1942 => [ 7.6, 26.4 ],                                    
      312 +     },                                                        
      313 +     color         => [ 'blue', 'gray' ],    # index 0, index 1
      314 +     label         => [ 'UK',   'US'   ],    # legend entries  
      315 +    );                                                        
      316 +                                                              
      317 +**3. Groups of bars (hash of hashes).** The same picture as (2
          +), but the series                                             
      318 +are named by the inner keys rather than by position, so no `la
          +bel` is needed:                                               
      319 +                                                              
      320 +    bar(                                                      
      321 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/grouped.hoh.svg',                  
      322 +     data          => {                                        
      323 +             1941 => { UK => 6.6, US => 6.2 },                         
      324 +             1942 => { UK => 7.6, US => 26.4 },                        
      325 +     },                                                        
      326 +    );                                                        
      327 +                                                              
      328 +Both grouped forms accept `stacked => 1` to pile the series on
          + top of one                                                   
      329 +another instead of placing them side by side.                 
      330 +                                                              
      331 +### Error bars                                                
      332 +                                                              
      333 +`yerr` (natural for `bar`) and `xerr` (natural for `barh`) tak
          +e either one                                                  
      334 +number for every bar, or a hash keyed by the data keys.  A two
          +-element array                                                
      335 +gives asymmetric `[ lower, upper ]` errors:                   
      336 +                                                              
      337 +    bar(                                                      
      338 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/warheads.svg',                     
      339 +     data          => { USA => 5277, Russia => 5449 },         
      340 +     yerr          => {                                        
      341 +             USA    => [ 15,  29   ],    # -15, +29                    
      342 +             Russia => [ 199, 1000 ],                                  
      343 +     },                                                        
      344 +     log           => 'True',                                  
      345 +     ylabel        => '# of Nuclear Warheads',                 
      346 +    );                                                        
      347 +                                                              
      348  ### Options
      349  
      350  | Option | Description | Example |

