      586  
      587  ## boxplot
      588  
      589 -Plot a hash of arrays as a series of boxplots                 
      589 +Plot a hash of arrays as a series of boxplots: one box per key
          +, labelled with                                               
      590 +the key and the number of points it holds.                    
      591  
      592 +### Entering data                                             
      593 +                                                              
      594 +Ordinarily `data` is a hash of array refs, one array per box: 
      595 +                                                              
      596 +    boxplot(                                                  
      597 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/boxes.svg',                        
      598 +     data          => { A => \@a, B => \@b, C => \@c },        
      599 +    );                                                        
      600 +                                                              
      601 +A bare array ref is the one-box shorthand; the box gets an emp
          +ty label:                                                     
      602 +                                                              
      603 +    boxplot(                                                  
      604 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/one.box.svg',                      
      605 +     data          => \@a,                                     
      606 +    );                                                        
      607 +                                                              
      608 +Values that are undefined or non-numeric are dropped rather th
          +an fatal, so a                                                
      609 +column read straight out of a spreadsheet with blank cells can
          + be handed over                                               
      610 +as-is.  `violin` takes exactly the same two shapes, which make
          +s swapping                                                    
      611 +`'plot.type' => 'boxplot'` for `'plot.type' => 'violinplot'` a
          + one-word change.                                             
      612 +                                                              
      613  ### options
      614  
      615  | Option | Description | Example |
      616  | -------- | ------- | ------- |
      595 -|`color` | a single color for all plots | `color => 'pink'`|  
      596 -|`colors`| a hash, where each data point and color is a hash p
          -air |`colors => { A => 'orange', E => 'yellow', B => 'purple' 
          -},`|                                                          
      597 -| `key.order`| order that the keys in the entry hash will be p
          -lotted | `key.order = ['A', 'E', 'B']` |                      
      598 -| `orientation`| orientation of the plot, by default `vertical
          -`| `orientation = 'horizontal'` |                             
      617 +|`color` | a single color for all boxes | `color => 'pink'`|  
      618 +|`colors`| a hash pairing each data key with its own color.  E
          +very key in `data` must appear, otherwise the call dies naming
          + the keys that have no color |`colors => { A => 'orange', E =>
          + 'yellow', B => 'purple' },`|                                 
      619 +| `key.order`| order that the keys in the entry hash will be p
          +lotted | `'key.order' => ['A', 'E', 'B']` |                   
      620 +|`logscale`| an array of the axes to put on a log scale; only 
          +`x` and `y` are accepted | `logscale => ['y']` |              
      621 +|`notch`| draw a notched box (`'True'`) instead of a rectangul
          +ar one | `notch => 'True'` |                                  
      622 +| `orientation`| orientation of the plot, by default `vertical
          +`| `orientation => 'horizontal'` |                            
      623  |`showcaps`| Show the caps on the ends of whiskers; default `T
           rue` | `showcaps => 'False',` |
      624  | `showfliers` |Show the outliers beyond the caps; default `Tr
           ue` | `showfliers  => 'False'` |
      625  |`showmeans` | show means; default = `True` | `showmeans   => 
           'False'` |
      602 -|`whiskers`| show whiskers, default = 1| ` whiskers    => 0,`|
      603 -                                                              
      626 +                                                              
      627 +`showcaps`, `showfliers`, `showmeans` and `notch` are passed s
          +traight through to                                            
      628 +Matplotlib, so they take Python's `'True'`/`'False'` rather th
          +an a Perl boolean.                                            
      629 +The `whiskers` switch belongs to [`violin`](#violin), not to `
          +boxplot`.                                                     
      630 +                                                              
