      787  
      788  ## Colored Table
      789  
      790 +Plot a hash of hashes as a matrix, coloring each cell by its v
          +alue.                                                         
      791 +                                                              
      792 +### Entering data                                             
      793 +                                                              
      794 +`data` is a hash of hashes: the outer key is the row, the inne
          +r key is the                                                  
      795 +column, and the value is the number that picks the cell's colo
          +r.                                                            
      796 +                                                              
      797 +    colored_table(                                            
      798 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/matrix.svg',                       
      799 +     data          => {                                        
      800 +             H => { H => 432, Cl => 427, Br => 363 },                
      801 +             C => { H => 413, Cl => 339, Br => 276 },                
      802 +     },                                                        
      803 +    );                                                        
      804 +                                                              
      805 +The matrix does not have to be complete.  Cells with no value 
          +are drawn in                                                  
      806 +`undef.color` (or given a number by `default_undefined`), and 
          +a table that only                                             
      807 +fills one triangle — the usual shape of a pairwise-comparison 
          +table — can be                                                
      808 +completed by reflecting it across the diagonal with `mirror =>
          + 1`, so that                                                  
      809 +`$data{A}{B}` also supplies `$data{B}{A}`.                    
      810 +                                                              
      811 +Rows and columns are otherwise sorted; `row.labels` and `col.l
          +abels` fix both                                               
      812 +the order and the subset that is drawn, which is how the bond-
          +dissociation                                                  
      813 +example below shows the halogens only.                        
      814 +                                                              
      815  ### options
      816  
      817 +| Option | Description | Example |                            
      818 +| -------- | ------- | ------- |                              
      819 +|`cb_logscale`| color the cells on a log scale | `cb_logscale 
          +=> 1` |                                                       
      820 +|`cb_min`, `cb_max`| clamp the ends of the color scale instead
          + of taking them from the data, so several tables can be compar
          +ed directly | `cb_min => 100, cb_max => 500` |                
      821 +|`cblabel`| the label on the colorbar | `cblabel => 'kJ/mol'` 
          +|                                                             
      822 +|`cmap`| the colormap used for coloring the cells | `cmap => '
          +viridis'` |                                                   
      823 +|`col.labels`| array ref: which columns to draw, in order | `'
          +col.labels' => ['H', 'F', 'Cl', 'Br', 'I']` |                 
      824 +|`colorbar.on`| draw the colorbar; on by default, `0` turns it
          + off | `'colorbar.on' => 0` |                                 
      825 +|`default_undefined`| the number to substitute wherever a cell
          + is missing, instead of leaving it uncolored | `default_undefi
          +ned => 0` |                                                   
      826 +|`logscale`| an array of the axes to put on a log scale | `log
          +scale => ['y']` |                                             
      827 +|`mirror`| treat the table as symmetric: `$data{A}{B}` also fi
          +lls `$data{B}{A}` | `mirror => 1` |                           
      828 +|`row.labels`| array ref: which rows to draw, in order | `'row
          +.labels' => ['H', 'F', 'Cl', 'Br', 'I']` |                    
      829 +|`shared.colorbar`| 0-based indices of the subplots that shoul
          +d share one colorbar | `'shared.colorbar' => [0,1]` |         
      830 +|`show.numbers`| print each cell's value in the cell; off by d
          +efault | `'show.numbers' => 1` |                              
      831 +|`undef.color`| the color for cells that have no value | `'und
          +ef.color' => 'white'` |                                       
      832 +                                                              
      833 +The colorbar options in [Color Bars](#color-bars-colorbars) — 
          +`cbdrawedges`,                                                
      834 +`cblocation`, `cborientation`, `cbpad` — work here too.       
      835 +                                                              
