      942  Plot a hash of arrays as a hexbin
      943  see https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/_as_gen/matplotlib.pyplo
           t.hexbin.html
      944  
      945 +A hexbin answers the question a scatterplot stops answering on
          +ce there are tens                                             
      946 +of thousands of points: instead of drawing every point and let
          +ting them pile up                                             
      947 +into an indistinguishable blob, the plane is tiled with hexago
          +ns and each one is                                            
      948 +colored by how many points fell inside it.                    
      949 +                                                              
      950 +### Entering data                                             
      951 +                                                              
      952 +`data` is a hash of exactly **two** array refs of equal length
          + — the first key                                              
      953 +(sorted) is the x-axis, the second is the y-axis, and both bec
          +ome the axis                                                  
      954 +labels.  Use `key.order` to say which is which rather than rel
          +ying on the sort:                                             
      955 +                                                              
      956 +    hexbin(                                                   
      957 +     'output.file' => '/tmp/hex.svg',                          
      958 +     data          => { Height => \@heights, Weight => \@weight
          +s },                                                          
      959 +     'key.order'   => [ 'Weight', 'Height' ],    # Weight on x 
      960 +     cblabel       => 'people per cell',                       
      961 +    );                                                        
      962 +                                                              
      963  ### options
      964  
      965  | Option | Description | Example |
      966  | -------- | ------- | ------- 
      967  | cb_logscale | colorbar log scale `from matplotlib.colors imp
           ort LogNorm` | default 0, any value > 0 enables |
      968 +| cblabel | the label on the colorbar, i.e. what the cell coun
          +ts mean | `cblabel => 'observations'` |                       
      969 +| colorbar.on | draw the colorbar; on by default, `0` turns it
          + off | `'colorbar.on' => 0` |                                 
      970 +| shared.colorbar | 0-based indices of the subplots that shoul
          +d share one colorbar, so that their colors are comparable | `'
          +shared.colorbar' => [0,1]` |                                  
      971  |cmap| The Colormap instance or registered colormap name used 
           to map scalar data to colors | default `gist_rainbow` |
      972  |key.order|  define the keys in an order (an array reference)|
           `'key.order' => ['X-rays', 'Yak Butter'],`
      973  | marginals | integer, by default off = 0 | `marginals => 1` |

