      1669  
      1670  ## pie
      1671  
      1672 +Plot a hash of numbers as a pie chart: one wedge per key, siz
           +ed by its share of                                           
      1673 +the total.  `data` is the same simple hash that `bar` takes, 
           +so the two are                                               
      1674 +interchangeable — reach for `pie` when the reader should see 
           +parts of a whole,                                            
      1675 +and for `bar` when they should compare the parts with each ot
           +her.                                                         
      1676 +                                                             
      1677 +Wedges are laid out in sorted key order and that order cannot
           + be overridden;                                              
      1678 +`key.order` is not accepted here.  Pie charts also never get 
           +a legend — the                                               
      1679 +wedges are labelled directly — so `legend` and `show.legend` 
           +do nothing.                                                  
      1680 +                                                             
      1681  ### options
      1682  
      1683 +| Option | Description | Example |                           
      1684 +| -------- | ------- | ------- |                             
      1685 +|`autopct`| a Python format string for the share printed insi
           +de each wedge; omit it and no numbers are drawn | `autopct =>
           + '%1.1f%%'` |                                                
      1686 +|`labeldistance`| where the key label sits, as a fraction of 
           +the radius: `0` is the centre, `1` the edge, above `1` outsid
           +e the pie | `labeldistance => 0.6` |                         
      1687 +|`pctdistance`| the same scale, for the `autopct` text.  Swap
           +ping the two — labels in, percentages out — is a readable arr
           +angement when the labels are long | `pctdistance => 1.25` |  
      1688 +                                                             
      1689  ### single, simple plot
      1690  
      1691      plt(

