      2385  
      2386  ## violin
      2387  
      2388 -plot a hash of array refs as violins                         
      2388 +Plot a hash of array refs as violins: one kernel-density silh
           +ouette per key, with                                         
      2389 +the quartile box, the whiskers and a red dot at the mean draw
           +n over it.  Where a                                          
      2390 +boxplot summarises a distribution in five numbers, a violin s
           +hows its shape, so                                           
      2391 +bimodal data that a boxplot would hide is visible.           
      2392  
      2393 +`violin` and `violinplot` are the same subroutine under two n
           +ames, and both                                               
      2394 +accept the two data shapes described under [boxplot](#boxplot
           +) — a hash of array                                          
      2395 +refs, or a bare array ref for a single violin.  Non-numeric a
           +nd undefined values                                          
      2396 +are dropped silently.  Each x-axis label carries the number o
           +f points that went                                           
      2397 +into it, so a violin drawn from very few points announces its
           +elf.                                                         
      2398 +                                                             
      2399  ### options
      2400  
      2401  | Option | Description | Example |
      2402  | -------- | ------- | -------
      2394 -|`color`| # a hash, where keys are the keys in data, and valu
           -es are colors, e.g. X => 'blue'                              
      2395 -|`colors`| match sets | `colors       => { E => 'yellow', B =
           -> 'purple', A => 'green' }`|                                 
      2396 -|`key.order`| determine key order display on x-axis|         
      2397 -|`log`|    # if set to > 1, the y-axis will be logarithmic   
      2398 -|`orientation`|'vertical', 'horizontal'}, default: 'vertical'
           -|                                                            
      2403 +|`color`| a single color for every violin |`color => 'red'`| 
      2404 +|`colors`| a hash pairing each data key with its own color; e
           +very key in `data` must appear | `colors       => { E => 'yel
           +low', B => 'purple', A => 'green' }`|                        
      2405 +|`key.order`| determine key order display on x-axis|`'key.ord
           +er' => ['B', 'A', 'E']`|                                     
      2406 +|`logscale`| an array of the axes to put on a log scale; only
           + `x` and `y` are accepted.  Note this is an array reference, 
           +not the `log => 1` scalar that `bar` takes |`logscale => ['y'
           +]`|                                                          
      2407 +|`orientation`|'vertical', 'horizontal'}, default: 'vertical'
           +|`orientation => 'horizontal'`|                              
      2408 +|`whiskers`| draw the quartile bar and whiskers over the silh
           +ouette; on by default, `0` leaves the bare violin |`whiskers 
           +=> 0`|                                                       
      2409  
