      2501  
      2502  ## wide
      2503 +                                                             
      2504 +Summarise **several runs of the same curve**.  Every run is d
           +rawn as a faint                                              
      2505 +line, the mean of the runs as a solid one, and one standard d
           +eviation either side                                         
      2506 +of the mean as a translucent ribbon.  This is the plot for re
           +peated measurements                                          
      2507 +— replicate experiments, repeated simulations, one trace per 
           +subject — where a                                            
      2508 +`plot` of every line on top of the others would be an unreada
           +ble thicket and a                                            
      2509 +`plot` of the mean alone would hide how much the runs disagre
           +e.                                                           
      2510 +                                                             
      2511 +The runs do not have to share an x grid: each group's runs ar
           +e interpolated onto                                          
      2512 +101 evenly spaced points spanning that group's own x range be
           +fore the mean and                                            
      2513 +the standard deviation are taken, so runs of different length
           +s, or sampled at                                             
      2514 +different x values, can be summarised together.              
      2515 +                                                             
      2516 +### Entering data                                            
      2517 +                                                             
      2518 +**1. Labelled groups (hash).** Each key is a group and become
           +s the legend label;                                          
      2519 +its value is an array of runs, and each run is a `[ \@x, \@y 
           +]` pair — the same                                           
      2520 +pair `plot` uses:                                            
      2521 +                                                             
      2522 +    my @x = 0 .. 100;                                        
      2523 +    wide(                                                    
      2524 +            'output.file' => 'output.images/single.wide.png',       
      2525 +            data          => {                                      
      2526 +                    Clinical => [                                   
      2527 +                            [ [@x], [@y1] ],    # run 1             
      2528 +                            [ [@x], [@y2] ],    # run 2             
      2529 +                            [ [@x], [@y3] ],    # run 3             
      2530 +                    ],                                              
      2531 +                    HGI => [                                        
      2532 +                            [ [@x], [@z1] ],                        
      2533 +                            [ [@x], [@z2] ],                        
      2534 +                    ],                                              
      2535 +            },                                                      
      2536 +            color         => {          # one color per group       
      2537 +                    Clinical => 'blue',                             
      2538 +                    HGI      => 'green',                            
      2539 +            },                                                      
      2540 +            title         => 'Visualization of similar lines plotted
           +together',                                                   
      2541 +    );                                                       
      2542 +                                                             
      2543 +**2. One unlabelled group (array).** Drop the enclosing hash 
           +and pass the array                                           
      2544 +of runs directly; `color` is then a single color rather than 
           +a hash:                                                      
      2545 +                                                             
      2546 +    wide(                                                    
      2547 +            'output.file' => 'output.images/single.array.png',      
      2548 +            data          => [                                      
      2549 +                    [ [@x], [@y1] ],                                
      2550 +                    [ [@x], [@y2] ],                                
      2551 +                    [ [@x], [@y3] ],                                
      2552 +            ],                                                      
      2553 +            color         => 'red',                                 
      2554 +    );                                                       
      2555 +                                                             
      2556 +A group with a single run is legal — it just produces a line 
           +with a                                                       
      2557 +zero-width ribbon — which is convenient when one group has re
           +plicates and                                                 
      2558 +another does not.                                            
      2559 +                                                             
      2560  ### options
      2561 +                                                             
      2562 +| Option | Description | Example |                           
      2563 +| -------- | ------- | ------- |                             
      2564 +|`color`| for hash data, a hash of one color per group; for a
           +rray data, a single color.  Groups with no entry fall back to
           + Matplotlib's `b` (blue), so a partial hash is allowed | `col
           +or => { Clinical => 'blue', HGI => 'green' }` |              
      2565 +|`show.legend`| on by default, and only the hash form has lab
           +els to show; `0` suppresses it | `'show.legend' => 0` |      
      2566 +                                                             
      2567 +`wide` accepts the usual axes options — `title`, `xlabel`, `y
           +label`, `set_xlim`                                           
      2568 +and the rest — but **not** `logscale` or `key.order`: use Mat
           +plotlib's own                                                
      2569 +`set_yscale => '"log"'` for a log axis, and note that the gro
           +ups are drawn in                                             
      2570 +hash order.                                                  
      2571 +                                                             
      2572  ### single, simple plot
      2573 +                                                             
      2574 +The two calls above each produce one panel.  Since `wide` is 
           +a `plt` wrapper, the                                         
      2575 +same hash works as an element of `plots`:                    
      2576 +                                                             
      2577 +    plt(                                                     
      2578 +            'output.file' => 'output.images/wide.png',              
      2579 +            ncols         => 2,                                     
      2580 +            suptitle      => 'Replicate runs, summarised',          
      2581 +            plots         => [                                      
      2582 +                    {                                               
      2583 +                            'plot.type' => 'wide',                  
      2584 +                            data        => \%runs,      # hash of gr
      2585 +                            color       => { Clinical => 'blue', HGI
      2586 +                            title       => 'Two groups, mean +/- 1 s
      2587 +                            xlabel      => 'time',                  
      2588 +                            ylabel      => 'signal',                
      2589 +                    },                                              
      2590 +                    {                                               
      2591 +                            'plot.type'   => 'wide',                
      2592 +                            data          => $runs{Clinical},    # j
           +abelled                                                      
      2593 +                            color         => 'red',                 
      2594 +                            'show.legend' => 0,                     
      2595 +                            title         => 'One group, no legend',
      2596 +                    },                                              
      2597 +            ],                                                      
      2598 +    );                                                       
      2599 +                                                             
      2600  ### multiple plots
      2601 +                                                             
      2602 +Because a `wide` panel collapses many lines into one summary,
           + it composes well                                            
      2603 +with the plot types that show the same data another way.  Her
           +e the runs are                                               
      2604 +summarised on the left and their endpoint distribution is dra
           +wn beside them:                                              
      2605 +                                                             
      2606 +    plt(                                                     
      2607 +            'output.file' => 'output.images/wide.and.violin.png',   
      2608 +            ncols         => 2,                                     
      2609 +            plots         => [                                      
      2610 +                    {                                               
      2611 +                            'plot.type' => 'wide',                  
      2612 +                            data        => \%runs,                  
      2613 +                            color       => { Clinical => 'blue', HGI
      2614 +                            title       => 'Runs over time',        
      2615 +                    },                                              
      2616 +                    {                                               
      2617 +                            'plot.type' => 'violinplot',            
      2618 +                            data        => \%endpoints,    # hash of
           +s                                                            
      2619 +                            colors      => { Clinical => 'blue', HGI
      2620 +                            title       => 'Final values',          
      2621 +                    },                                              
      2622 +            ],                                                      
      2623 +    );                                                       
      2624 +                                                             
      2625  # Advanced
      2626  ## Notes in Files
      2627  
