● Update(README.md)
  ⎿  Added 35 lines
      1907  Common axes options such as `title`, `xlabel`, `ylabel`, and 
            `legend` are
      1908  accepted here too, exactly as for the other plot types.
      1909  
      1910 +### Two y-axes with `twinx`                                  
      1911 +                                                             
      1912 +Series measured in different units, or on wildly different sc
           +ales, flatten each                                           
      1913 +other when they share a y-axis.  `twinx` moves the named seri
           +es onto a second                                             
      1914 +y-axis on the right, and `twinx.args` labels it:             
      1915 +                                                             
      1916 +    plt(                                                     
      1917 +            'output.file' => '/tmp/twinx.svg',                       
      1918 +            'plot.type'   => 'plot',                                 
      1919 +            data          => {                                       
      1920 +                    Temperature => [ [@t], [@celsius] ],                     
      1921 +                    Pressure    => [ [@t], [@hPa]     ],                     
      1922 +            },                                                       
      1923 +            twinx         => 'Pressure',                        # ont
           +o the right axis                                             
      1924 +            'twinx.args'  => { Pressure => { ylabel => 'hPa' } },    
      1925 +            ylabel        => 'degrees C',                       # the
           + left axis                                                   
      1926 +            xlabel        => 'hour',                                 
      1927 +    );                                                       
      1928 +                                                             
      1929 +`twinx => 'Pressure'` is shorthand for the single-series case
           +; to twin more than                                          
      1930 +one series, pass a hash whose keys are the series to move — `
           +twinx => { Pressure                                          
      1931 +=> 1, Humidity => 1 }`.  With array data the same options are
           + given by index                                              
      1932 +instead of by key:                                           
      1933 +                                                             
      1934 +    plt(                                                     
      1935 +            'output.file' => '/tmp/twinx.arr.svg',                   
      1936 +            'plot.type'   => 'plot',                                 
      1937 +            data          => [                                       
      1938 +                    [ [@t], [@celsius] ],    # index 0, left axis            
      1939 +                    [ [@t], [@hPa]     ],    # index 1                       
      1940 +            ],                                                       
      1941 +            twinx         => 1,                              # index 
           +1 goes right                                                 
      1942 +            'twinx.args'  => { 1 => { ylabel => 'hPa' } },           
      1943 +    );                                                       
      1944 +                                                             
      1945  A `plot` spec is an ordinary plot hash, so it can be dropped 
            straight into the
      1946  [`p`](#the-p-argument) argument — on its own for a single sub
            plot, or alongside
      1947  other hashes to overlay or to fill a grid of subplots.

