      178  
      179  `sharex` and `sharey` are both implemented at the plot, rather
            than subplot, level.  See Matplotlib's documentation for more
            clarity.
      180  
      181 +### Quoting text: commas and apostrophes                      
      182 +                                                              
      183 +`title`, `suptitle`, `xlabel`, `ylabel`, `set_title`, `set_xla
          +bel` and                                                      
      184 +`set_ylabel` are quoted for you — but only when the text conta
          +ins no comma, no                                              
      185 +apostrophe and no double quote.  Anything else is passed throu
          +gh to Python                                                  
      186 +untouched, on the assumption that you are supplying Python syn
          +tax of your own,                                              
      187 +which is what makes a raw string such as                      
      188 +                                                              
      189 +    xlabel => 'r"$\it{anno}$ $\it{domini}$"',    # italics, vi
          +a mathtext                                                    
      190 +                                                              
      191 +possible in the first place.  The practical consequence is tha
          +t a plain-English                                             
      192 +label with a comma or an apostrophe in it has to carry its own
          + quotes:                                                      
      193 +                                                              
      194 +    title => 'Two groups: mean and s.d.',     # fine, no comma
      195 +    title => '"Two groups, mean and s.d."',   # comma: quote i
          +t yourself                                                    
      196 +    title => '"war\'s end"',                  # apostrophe: li
          +kewise                                                        
      197 +                                                              
      198 +Without those quotes the generated Python is a syntax error ra
          +ther than a                                                   
      199 +mislabelled plot, so the mistake is loud.  Every other option 
          +is passed through                                             
      200 +as written, so text inside `legend`, `text` and friends is Pyt
          +hon syntax                                                    
      201 +throughout: `legend => 'loc = "upper left"'`.                 
      202 +                                                              
      203  # Color Bars (colorbars)
      204  
      205  Colarbar args attempt to match matplotlib closely

