      1145  
      1146  ## hist
      1147  
      1148 -Plot a hash of arrays as a series of histograms.  Every set i
           -s drawn into the                                             
      1149 -same axes with a shared bin edge, so the point of `hist` is c
           -omparing                                                     
      1150 -distributions; `alpha` defaults to 0.5 so that the overlaps s
           -tay readable.                                                
      1148 +Plot a hash of arrays as a series of histograms, one per key,
           + drawn over each                                             
      1149 +other in the same axes — `alpha` defaults to 0.5 so that the 
           +overlaps stay                                                
      1150 +readable.  A single array ref is the one-set shorthand.  Valu
           +es must be numeric:                                          
      1151 +unlike `boxplot` and `violin`, a non-numeric value here is an
           + error.                                                      
      1152  
      1153 +Each set is binned separately, so with `bins => 50` two sets 
           +covering different                                           
      1154 +ranges get 50 bins each over their own range rather than a co
           +mmon set of edges.                                           
      1155 +When the sets must line up exactly — which is what makes the 
           +bar heights                                                  
      1156 +comparable — pass the edges themselves rather than a count:  
      1157 +                                                             
      1158 +    hist(                                                    
      1159 +            'output.file' => '/tmp/hist.svg',                        
      1160 +            data          => { E => \@e, B => \@b },                 
      1161 +            bins          => [ map { 10 * $_ } 0 .. 20 ],    # shared
           + edges, 0..200                                               
      1162 +    );                                                       
      1163 +                                                             
      1164 +`bins` and `color` also accept a **hash keyed by set**, for w
           +hen one                                                      
      1165 +distribution wants different treatment from the others:      
      1166 +                                                             
      1167 +            bins  => { E => 50, B => 20 },                           
      1168 +            color => { E => 'orange', B => 'black' },                
      1169 +                                                             
      1170 +The legend is on by default when there is more than one set a
           +nd off when there is                                         
      1171 +only one; `show.legend` overrides that either way.           
      1172 +                                                             
      1173  ### options
      1174  
      1175  | Option | Description | Example |

