● Done. The README grew by ~600 lines, and everything documented was verified by
  running it.

  What each helper gained

  ┌───────────┬────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  Helper   │   Before   │                      Now                       │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │           │ 4 empty    │ Full section: what the plot is (faint runs +   │
  │ wide      │ headings   │ mean + ±1 s.d. ribbon), both data shapes,      │
  │           │            │ interpolation behaviour, options, 4 examples   │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │           │ empty ###  │ Both data shapes (2/3-key hash;                │
  │ scatter   │ options    │ hash-of-hashes), the x/y/colour role rules,    │
  │           │            │ keys vs color_key, full options table          │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ pie       │ empty ###  │ Intro, options table (autopct, labeldistance,  │
  │           │ options    │ pctdistance)                                   │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Colored   │ empty ###  │ Data shape, mirror, missing-cell behaviour,    │
  │ Table     │ options    │ 11-row options table                           │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ bar/barh  │ options    │ "Entering data" (3 shapes), "Error bars",      │
  │           │ only       │ label + logscale rows                          │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ hist      │ 5 thin     │ Per-set binning trap + shared-edge fix,        │
  │           │ rows       │ per-set bins/color hashes, legend defaults     │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ boxplot   │ options    │ Data shapes, logscale/notch rows               │
  │           │ only       │                                                │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ imshow    │ 7 rows     │ Data shape, origin/row-order, stringmap        │
  │           │            │ semantics, 4 new rows                          │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ hexbin,   │ options    │ What the plot is for, data shape,              │
  │ hist2d    │ only       │ cblabel/cmin/density explained,                │
  │           │            │ cb_logscale+vmin conflict                      │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ violin    │ 5 thin     │ Intro contrasting it with boxplot, corrected   │
  │           │ rows       │ options                                        │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ plot      │ already    │ New "Two y-axes with twinx" section — the      │
  │           │ strong     │ option was documented but never shown          │
  └───────────┴────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Plus two cross-cutting additions: a "Which helper takes which data?" table
  indexing every plot type by the Perl data shape you already have, and "Quoting
  text: commas and apostrophes" under Options.

  Errors found and fixed

  The docs claimed four things the code rejects. I probed 119 option/shape
  combinations against the real module to find them:

  - boxplot's whiskers — belongs to violin; boxplot dies on it. Replaced with
  logscale.
  - violin's and hist's log — both die; the option is logscale => ['y'] (an
  array ref, not a scalar — bar's is a scalar, which is now stated).
  - The scatter multi-set example's color_key => 'Z' against inner keys A,B,C —
  dies with "Z" isn't defined for set "X". Now color_key => 'C'.

  The comma rule surfaced from my own examples failing: title => 'Two groups, 
  mean' generates ax.set_title(Two groups, mean), a Python SyntaxError.
  Auto-quoting is skipped whenever the text contains a comma, apostrophe or
  double quote — that's what lets xlabel => 'r"$\it{anno}$"' work, and it's now
  documented with the workaround.

  Verified

  - 22 README examples run verbatim (/tmp/readme.out), including all wide and
  twinx snippets.
  - perl md2pod.pl regenerates README.pod and the module POD cleanly — POD test
  ok, Changes byte-identical. One POD break I hit along the way (a backticked
  span wrapped across lines, whose continuation started =>, which the POD-repair
  pass read as a command paragraph) is fixed.
  - prove t/*.t: 208 tests pass; 5.10.1 still compiles.

  Options that exist in code but don't work

  Not documented, since documenting them would be documenting a bug — but you
  may want to look at them:

  - violin: medians and edgecolor are read and defaulted, but absent from %opt,
  so passing either dies. edgecolor is also never used — set_edgecolor('black')
  is hardcoded.
  - pie: key.order is read by pie_helper but not registered, so it dies both at
  top level and inside plots.
  - colored_table: default_undefined is defaulted, but the line that used it is
  commented out — cells always become np.nan.
  - colorbar.on is honoured by imshow and colored_table, but ignored by hexbin
  and hist2d (they always draw; only show.colorbar suppresses hist2d). scatter
  ignores colorbar.on, show.legend and shared.colorbar entirely.

